2025-08-12 16:42:03,285 - root - DEBUG - Sefaria's Search API response: {"took": 94, "timed_out": false, "_shards": {"total": 1, "successful": 1, "skipped": 0, "failed": 0}, "hits": {"total": 181, "max_score": 424456.28, "hits": [{"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Exodus 21:26 (The Kehot Chumash; Chabad House Publications, Los Angeles [en])", "_score": 424456.28, "_source": {"ref": "Exodus 21:26", "heRef": "שמות כ״א:כ״ו", "version": "The Kehot Chumash; Chabad House Publications, Los Angeles", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 4, "titleVariants": ["Exod.", "Ex.", "Exo", "Shmot", "Shemot", "Ex", "Exo.", "Exod", "Shemoth", "Shemos", "Exodus"], "categories": ["Tanakh", "Torah"], "order": "A00000000100210026", "path": "Tanakh/Torah/Exodus", "pagesheetrank": 29528.755957404624, "comp_date": -1400, "exact": " The Non-Jewish Bondservant, continued The law of release after six years, at the Jubilee year, or upon the onset of puberty, does not apply to non-Jewish bondservants. They serve for life or for the term for which they were bought, unless someone pays for their release or their master frees them. When their master frees them, they become full Israelites. If , however, a person strikes the eye of his non-Jewish bondman or the eye of his non-Jewish bondwoman and ruins his eyesight , he must free him or her as compensation for the loss of his or her eye . The same applies if the master strikes and destroys any of the bondservant’s fingers, toes, ears, nose, or his reproductive organ. 45 Mishneh Torah, Isurei Bi’ah 13:12; cf. Rashi on Leviticus 19:20.", "naive_lemmatizer": " The Non-Jewish Bondservant, continued The law of release after six years, at the Jubilee year, or upon the onset of puberty, does not apply to non-Jewish bondservants. They serve for life or for the term for which they were bought, unless someone pays for their release or their master frees them. When their master frees them, they become full Israelites. If , however, a person strikes the eye of his non-Jewish bondman or the eye of his non-Jewish bondwoman and ruins his eyesight , he must free him or her as compensation for the loss of his or her eye . The same applies if the master strikes and destroys any of the bondservant’s fingers, toes, ears, nose, or his reproductive organ. 45 Mishneh Torah, Isurei Bi’ah 13:12; cf. Rashi on Leviticus 19:20.", "hebrew_version_title": null, "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["The same applies if the master strikes and destroys any of the bondservant’s fingers, <b>toes</b>, ears, nose, or his reproductive organ. 45 Mishneh Torah, Isurei Bi’ah 13:12; cf. Rashi on Leviticus 19:20."]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Mishnah Chullin 3:6 (Sefaria Community Translation [en])", "_score": 61789.098, "_source": {"ref": "Mishnah Chullin 3:6", "heRef": "משנה חולין ג׳:ו׳", "version": "Sefaria Community Translation", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 4, "titleVariants": ["M. Chullin", "Mishna Chullin", "M Chullin", "Mishnah Ḥull.", "Mishnah Ḥullin", "Mishnah Chullin"], "categories": ["Mishnah", "Seder Kodashim"], "order": "A00100400200030006", "path": "Mishnah/Seder Kodashim/Mishnah Chullin", "pagesheetrank": 3659.088792567304, "comp_date": 190, "exact": "The signs of cattle and a wild animal are stated from the Torah, but the signs of a bird are not stated. But the Sages said, \"Any bird which attacks [prey] is prohibited. Any that has an extra digit, a crop, and gizzard that peels [away] is permitted.\" Rabbi Eliezer ben Rebbi Tzadok says, \"Every bird which parts its toes is prohibited.\"", "naive_lemmatizer": "The signs of cattle and a wild animal are stated from the Torah, but the signs of a bird are not stated. But the Sages said, \"Any bird which attacks [prey] is prohibited. Any that has an extra digit, a crop, and gizzard that peels [away] is permitted.\" Rabbi Eliezer ben Rebbi Tzadok says, \"Every bird which parts its toes is prohibited.\"", "hebrew_version_title": "תרגום קהילת ספריא", "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["Rabbi Eliezer ben Rebbi Tzadok says, \"Every bird which parts its <b>toes</b> is prohibited.\""]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Mishnah Chullin 3:6 (Mishnah Yomit by Dr. Joshua Kulp [en])", "_score": 61225.934, "_source": {"ref": "Mishnah Chullin 3:6", "heRef": "משנה חולין ג׳:ו׳", "version": "Mishnah Yomit by Dr. Joshua Kulp", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 1, "titleVariants": ["M. Chullin", "Mishna Chullin", "M Chullin", "Mishnah Ḥull.", "Mishnah Ḥullin", "Mishnah Chullin"], "categories": ["Mishnah", "Seder Kodashim"], "order": "A00100400200030006", "path": "Mishnah/Seder Kodashim/Mishnah Chullin", "pagesheetrank": 3659.088792567304, "comp_date": 190, "exact": "The characteristics of cattle and of wild animals are stated in the Torah. The characteristics of birds are not stated, but the sages said: every bird that seizes its prey is unclean. Every bird that has an extra toe, or a crop and a gizzard that can be peeled, is clean. Rabbi Elazar bar Zadok says: every bird that parts its toes is unclean.", "naive_lemmatizer": "The characteristics of cattle and of wild animals are stated in the Torah. The characteristics of birds are not stated, but the sages said: every bird that seizes its prey is unclean. Every bird that has an extra toe, or a crop and a gizzard that can be peeled, is clean. Rabbi Elazar bar Zadok says: every bird that parts its toes is unclean.", "hebrew_version_title": null, "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["Rabbi Elazar bar Zadok says: every bird that parts its <b>toes</b> is unclean."]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Mishnah Chullin 3:6 (Eighteen Treatises from the Mishna [en])", "_score": 57065.05, "_source": {"ref": "Mishnah Chullin 3:6", "heRef": "משנה חולין ג׳:ו׳", "version": "Eighteen Treatises from the Mishna", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 5, "titleVariants": ["M. Chullin", "Mishna Chullin", "M Chullin", "Mishnah Ḥull.", "Mishnah Ḥullin", "Mishnah Chullin"], "categories": ["Mishnah", "Seder Kodashim"], "order": "A00100400200030006", "path": "Mishnah/Seder Kodashim/Mishnah Chullin", "pagesheetrank": 3659.088792567304, "comp_date": 190, "exact": "The signs by which the clean animals, domestic and wild, may be distinguished [from the unclean and prohibited ones] are mentioned in the Holy Law, but not those of fowl. The sages have, however, established, \"That every [predaceous] bird, which strikes its talons into its prey, is of the unclean: every bird which has an additional claw, a crop, and of which the internal coat of the stomach may be readily peeled off, is of the clean species.\" R. Eleazar ben Zadok saith, \"Every bird which [when placed on a perch] divides its toes equally, is an unclean one.\"", "naive_lemmatizer": "The signs by which the clean animals, domestic and wild, may be distinguished [from the unclean and prohibited ones] are mentioned in the Holy Law, but not those of fowl. The sages have, however, established, \"That every [predaceous] bird, which strikes its talons into its prey, is of the unclean: every bird which has an additional claw, a crop, and of which the internal coat of the stomach may be readily peeled off, is of the clean species.\" R. Eleazar ben Zadok saith, \"Every bird which [when placed on a perch] divides its toes equally, is an unclean one.\"", "hebrew_version_title": "שמונה עשרה מסכתות משנה", "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["Eleazar ben Zadok saith, \"Every bird which [when placed on a perch] divides its <b>toes</b> equally, is an unclean one.\""]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Judges 1:7 (The Metsudah Tanach series, Lakewood, N.J [en])", "_score": 43975.797, "_source": {"ref": "Judges 1:7", "heRef": "שופטים א׳:ז׳", "version": "The Metsudah Tanach series, Lakewood, N.J", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 2, "titleVariants": ["Shoftim", "Jdg", "Judg", "Jdg.", "Judg.", "Jud.", "Judices", "Shofetim", "Juges", "Judges"], "categories": ["Tanakh", "Prophets"], "order": "A00000100100010007", "path": "Tanakh/Prophets/Judges", "pagesheetrank": 2430.5370377268355, "comp_date": -1300, "exact": "Adonibezek said, \"Seventy kings with amputated thumbs and big toes were scavengers under my table. God has punished me according to my actions.\" They brought him to Yerushalayim, where he died.", "naive_lemmatizer": "Adonibezek said, \"Seventy kings with amputated thumbs and big toes were scavengers under my table. God has punished me according to my actions.\" They brought him to Yerushalayim, where he died.", "hebrew_version_title": null, "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["Adonibezek said, \"Seventy kings with amputated thumbs and big <b>toes</b> were scavengers under my table. God has punished me according to my actions.\" They brought him to Yerushalayim, where he died."]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Judges 1:7 (Sefaria Community Translation [en])", "_score": 43440.64, "_source": {"ref": "Judges 1:7", "heRef": "שופטים א׳:ז׳", "version": "Sefaria Community Translation", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 8, "titleVariants": ["Shoftim", "Jdg", "Judg", "Jdg.", "Judg.", "Jud.", "Judices", "Shofetim", "Juges", "Judges"], "categories": ["Tanakh", "Prophets"], "order": "A00000100100010007", "path": "Tanakh/Prophets/Judges", "pagesheetrank": 2430.5370377268355, "comp_date": -1300, "exact": "7 Adoni-Bezek said, \"The cut-off thumbs and toes of seventy kings were gathered under my table; like I have done, so God has repaid me.\" They brought him to Yerushalayim and he died there.", "naive_lemmatizer": "7 Adoni-Bezek said, \"The cut-off thumbs and toes of seventy kings were gathered under my table; like I have done, so God has repaid me.\" They brought him to Yerushalayim and he died there.", "hebrew_version_title": null, "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["7 Adoni-Bezek said, \"The cut-off thumbs and <b>toes</b> of seventy kings were gathered under my table; like I have done, so God has repaid me.\" They brought him to Yerushalayim and he died there."]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Judges 1:7 (THE JPS TANAKH: Gender-Sensitive Edition [en])", "_score": 43125.75, "_source": {"ref": "Judges 1:7", "heRef": "שופטים א׳:ז׳", "version": "THE JPS TANAKH: Gender-Sensitive Edition", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 0, "titleVariants": ["Shoftim", "Jdg", "Judg", "Jdg.", "Judg.", "Jud.", "Judices", "Shofetim", "Juges", "Judges"], "categories": ["Tanakh", "Prophets"], "order": "A00000100100010007", "path": "Tanakh/Prophets/Judges", "pagesheetrank": 2430.5370377268355, "comp_date": -1300, "exact": "And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big toes cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there.", "naive_lemmatizer": "And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big toes cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there.", "hebrew_version_title": null, "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big <b>toes</b> cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there."]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Judges 1:7 (Tanakh: The Holy Scriptures, published by JPS [en])", "_score": 43125.75, "_source": {"ref": "Judges 1:7", "heRef": "שופטים א׳:ז׳", "version": "Tanakh: The Holy Scriptures, published by JPS", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 1, "titleVariants": ["Shoftim", "Jdg", "Judg", "Jdg.", "Judg.", "Jud.", "Judices", "Shofetim", "Juges", "Judges"], "categories": ["Tanakh", "Prophets"], "order": "A00000100100010007", "path": "Tanakh/Prophets/Judges", "pagesheetrank": 2430.5370377268355, "comp_date": -1300, "exact": "And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big toes cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there.", "naive_lemmatizer": "And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big toes cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there.", "hebrew_version_title": null, "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big <b>toes</b> cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there."]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Judges 1:7 (The Koren Jerusalem Bible [en])", "_score": 43125.75, "_source": {"ref": "Judges 1:7", "heRef": "שופטים א׳:ז׳", "version": "The Koren Jerusalem Bible", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 5, "titleVariants": ["Shoftim", "Jdg", "Judg", "Jdg.", "Judg.", "Jud.", "Judices", "Shofetim", "Juges", "Judges"], "categories": ["Tanakh", "Prophets"], "order": "A00000100100010007", "path": "Tanakh/Prophets/Judges", "pagesheetrank": 2430.5370377268355, "comp_date": -1300, "exact": "And Adoni-bezeq said, Seventy kings, having their thumbs and their great toes cut off, gathered food under my table: as I have done, so God has requited me. And they brought him to Yerushalayim, and there he died.", "naive_lemmatizer": "And Adoni-bezeq said, Seventy kings, having their thumbs and their great toes cut off, gathered food under my table: as I have done, so God has requited me. And they brought him to Yerushalayim, and there he died.", "hebrew_version_title": null, "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["And Adoni-bezeq said, Seventy kings, having their thumbs and their great <b>toes</b> cut off, gathered food under my table: as I have done, so God has requited me."]}}, {"_index": "text-a", "_id": "Judges 1:7 (The Holy Scriptures: A New Translation (JPS 1917) [en])", "_score": 43021.805, "_source": {"ref": "Judges 1:7", "heRef": "שופטים א׳:ז׳", "version": "The Holy Scriptures: A New Translation (JPS 1917)", "lang": "en", "version_priority": 3, "titleVariants": ["Shoftim", "Jdg", "Judg", "Jdg.", "Judg.", "Jud.", "Judices", "Shofetim", "Juges", "Judges"], "categories": ["Tanakh", "Prophets"], "order": "A00000100100010007", "path": "Tanakh/Prophets/Judges", "pagesheetrank": 2430.5370377268355, "comp_date": -1300, "exact": "And Adoni-bezek said: ‘Threescore and ten kings, having their thumbs and their great toes cut off, gathered food under my table; as I have done, so God hath requited me.’ And they brought him to Jerusalem, and he died there.", "naive_lemmatizer": "And Adoni-bezek said: ‘Threescore and ten kings, having their thumbs and their great toes cut off, gathered food under my table; as I have done, so God hath requited me.’ And they brought him to Jerusalem, and he died there.", "hebrew_version_title": "כתבי הקודש: תרגום חדש (1917 JPS)", "languageFamilyName": "english", "isPrimary": false}, "highlight": {"naive_lemmatizer": ["And Adoni-bezek said: ‘Threescore and ten kings, having their thumbs and their great <b>toes</b> cut off, gathered food under my table; as I have done, so God hath requited me.’"]}}]}}
2025-08-12 16:42:03,285 - root - DEBUG - formated results: ['Reference: Exodus 21:26\n Hebrew Reference: שמות כ״א:כ״ו\n Highlight: The same applies if the master strikes and destroys any of the bondservant’s fingers, <b>toes</b>, ears, nose, or his reproductive organ. 45 Mishneh Torah, Isurei Bi’ah 13:12; cf. Rashi on Leviticus 19:20.\n', 'Reference: Mishnah Chullin 3:6\n Hebrew Reference: משנה חולין ג׳:ו׳\n Highlight: Rabbi Eliezer ben Rebbi Tzadok says, "Every bird which parts its <b>toes</b> is prohibited."\n', 'Reference: Mishnah Chullin 3:6\n Hebrew Reference: משנה חולין ג׳:ו׳\n Highlight: Rabbi Elazar bar Zadok says: every bird that parts its <b>toes</b> is unclean.\n', 'Reference: Mishnah Chullin 3:6\n Hebrew Reference: משנה חולין ג׳:ו׳\n Highlight: Eleazar ben Zadok saith, "Every bird which [when placed on a perch] divides its <b>toes</b> equally, is an unclean one."\n', 'Reference: Judges 1:7\n Hebrew Reference: שופטים א׳:ז׳\n Highlight: Adonibezek said, "Seventy kings with amputated thumbs and big <b>toes</b> were scavengers under my table. God has punished me according to my actions." They brought him to Yerushalayim, where he died.\n', 'Reference: Judges 1:7\n Hebrew Reference: שופטים א׳:ז׳\n Highlight: 7 Adoni-Bezek said, "The cut-off thumbs and <b>toes</b> of seventy kings were gathered under my table; like I have done, so God has repaid me." They brought him to Yerushalayim and he died there.\n', 'Reference: Judges 1:7\n Hebrew Reference: שופטים א׳:ז׳\n Highlight: And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big <b>toes</b> cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there.\n', 'Reference: Judges 1:7\n Hebrew Reference: שופטים א׳:ז׳\n Highlight: And Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings, with thumbs and big <b>toes</b> cut off, used to pick up scraps under my table; as I have done, so God has requited me.” They brought him to Jerusalem and he died there.\n', 'Reference: Judges 1:7\n Hebrew Reference: שופטים א׳:ז׳\n Highlight: And Adoni-bezeq said, Seventy kings, having their thumbs and their great <b>toes</b> cut off, gathered food under my table: as I have done, so God has requited me.\n', 'Reference: Judges 1:7\n Hebrew Reference: שופטים א׳:ז׳\n Highlight: And Adoni-bezek said: ‘Threescore and ten kings, having their thumbs and their great <b>toes</b> cut off, gathered food under my table; as I have done, so God hath requited me.’\n']
